that had happened that day and whatever else is top of mind.

1125
00:47:05.650 --> 00:47:07.928
And it was cool.

1126
00:47:07.928 --> 00:47:11.257
It's almost like it will become a museum.

1127
00:47:11.257 --> 00:47:14.130
It'll be interesting to see what it looks like

1128
00:47:14.130 --> 00:47:16.640
in a year or five years from now.

1129
00:47:16.640 --> 00:47:19.030
The context in Minneapolis of all of this,

1130
00:47:19.030 --> 00:47:24.030
like George Floyd's death was to put it in,

1131
00:47:24.300 --> 00:47:28.003
we've all seen the video, and we've heard about,

1132
00:47:30.100 --> 00:47:33.783
we know about Chauvin and his background and it was murder,

1133
00:47:35.530 --> 00:47:39.250
but he was one of many people who have been abused

1134
00:47:39.250 --> 00:47:42.650
or killed by the Minneapolis Police Department.

1135
00:47:42.650 --> 00:47:46.090
They've had long time accusations of racism.

1136
00:47:46.090 --> 00:47:47.970
Black residents are more likely to be pulled over,

1137
00:47:47.970 --> 00:47:50.900
arrested, roughed up than White citizens.

1138
00:47:50.900 --> 00:47:53.370
They account for 20% of the city's population,

1139
00:47:53.370 --> 00:47:55.390
but made up more than 60% of the victims

1140
00:47:55.390 --> 00:47:58.930
of city police shootings from 2009 to 2019,

1141
00:47:58.930 --> 00:48:00.640
according to police data.

1142
00:48:00.640 --> 00:48:02.970
And Merrick Garland, the attorney general,

1143
00:48:02.970 --> 00:48:05.080
has just announced a complete investigation

1144
00:48:05.080 --> 00:48:06.470
into the Minneapolis police force

1145
00:48:06.470 --> 00:48:10.680
with the blessing of the chief, who is Black, we should say.

1146
00:48:10.680 --> 00:48:14.280
And so all that is the context for you being there.

1147
00:48:14.280 --> 00:48:16.440
That's the context for George Floyd Square

1148
00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:18.470
kind of blooming and becoming this place.

1149
00:48:18.470 --> 00:48:21.213
Yeah, the context is much broader than George Floyd.

1150
00:48:22.080 --> 00:48:24.210
And that's something that, look,

1151
00:48:24.210 --> 00:48:27.400
I realize like emotions run high around this.

1152
00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:30.430
In my opinion, Derek Chauvin

1153
00:48:30.430 --> 00:48:33.250
snuffing the life out of this guy on video,

1154
00:48:33.250 --> 00:48:36.620
it's like, this is not a hard case.

1155
00:48:36.620 --> 00:48:38.530
No.
And it is interesting

1156
00:48:38.530 --> 00:48:41.040
that there was such an exhale

1157
00:48:41.040 --> 00:48:43.640
and a sigh of relief when the verdict was announced.

1158
00:48:44.740 --> 00:48:48.370
Because it seems like this should be a no brainer,

1159
00:48:48.370 --> 00:48:51.370
and yet time and time again, we've seen it go the other way.

1160
00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:56.550
It was interesting when I posted a little clip,

1161
00:48:56.550 --> 00:48:58.980
little video clip of me and the guys

1162
00:48:58.980 --> 00:49:02.710
walking through George Floyd Square on Instagram last week,

1163
00:49:02.710 --> 00:49:05.310
it was for the most part well received,

1164
00:49:05.310 --> 00:49:10.110
but also met with not a small amount of derision

1165
00:49:10.110 --> 00:49:13.860
and what I would characterize as moral confusion.

1166
00:49:13.860 --> 00:49:18.450
If you ad hominem attacks a lot of what-about-ism

1167
00:49:18.450 --> 00:49:22.500
and this idea that to honor that space

1168
00:49:22.500 --> 00:49:27.180
and to appreciate the movement is somehow

1169
00:49:27.180 --> 00:49:31.470
to hoist George Floyd up as some kind of hero,

1170
00:49:31.470 --> 00:49:33.610
which really misses the point

1171
00:49:33.610 --> 00:49:36.260
and the main issue of the whole thing.

1172
00:49:36.260 --> 00:49:38.650
It was dispiriting on some regard to see that.

1173
00:49:38.650 --> 00:49:40.510
And I understand everybody's got

1174
00:49:40.510 --> 00:49:43.040
their own take and opinion on that.

1175
00:49:43.040 --> 00:49:46.400
And ultimately, I'd do it again.

1176
00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:49.030
I feel pretty good about being on the right side of history.

1177
00:49:49.030 --> 00:49:52.150
And like I said, I'm proud of the work that we've done.

1178
00:49:52.150 --> 00:49:53.420
And I think it is important.

1179
00:49:53.420 --> 00:49:55.960
And I talked to Brogan about this the other day.

1180
00:49:55.960 --> 00:50:00.320
There's this idea that yes, we all saw the verdict.

1181
00:50:00.320 --> 00:50:04.400
We watched it live here in the studio the other day.

1182
00:50:04.400 --> 00:50:08.403
There is this sense that we can exhale a sense of relief.

1183
00:50:09.290 --> 00:50:14.290
And I think it's okay to be happy about it for a minute.

1184
00:50:15.440 --> 00:50:16.340
There's this sense, like,

1185
00:50:16.340 --> 00:50:18.290
well, we can't be happy about this,

1186
00:50:18.290 --> 00:50:20.000
there's so much work that has to be done.

1187
00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:21.763
And that's certainly true.
Yeah.

1188
00:50:24.050 --> 00:50:28.450
But I think we can be grateful

1189
00:50:28.450 --> 00:50:30.440
that it turned out in that way

1190
00:50:30.440 --> 00:50:32.460
without it being some kind of a referendum

1191
00:50:32.460 --> 00:50:35.540
on the extent of the remaining work to be done.

1192
00:50:35.540 --> 00:50:37.800
Yeah, I think so.

1193
00:50:37.800 --> 00:50:39.310
I think that what you were referencing

