00:52:51.770 --> 00:52:53.190
People should check out that episode

1236
00:52:53.190 --> 00:52:54.530
'cause it's very interesting.

1237
00:52:54.530 --> 00:52:57.810
But for me, from looking at it,

1238
00:52:57.810 --> 00:53:00.090
when I look at the effects

1239
00:53:00.090 --> 00:53:03.146
of the Black Lives Matter movement this summer,

1240
00:53:03.146 --> 00:53:04.740
now we see two things.

1241
00:53:04.740 --> 00:53:07.730
One is the Biden election victory.

1242
00:53:07.730 --> 00:53:09.560
I think that's still directly tied to that.

1243
00:53:09.560 --> 00:53:11.520
I don't think you have the turnout you have

1244
00:53:11.520 --> 00:53:13.320
for Biden without Black Lives Matter.

1245
00:53:13.320 --> 00:53:17.260
I think that's a big win that is connected completely.

1246
00:53:17.260 --> 00:53:19.100
I think that was the first.

1247
00:53:19.100 --> 00:53:20.990
And I think the George Floyd, first of all,

1248
00:53:20.990 --> 00:53:24.160
having a murder case at all, and then the verdict.

1249
00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:28.740
I do think that you got to give credit to the BLM movement.

1250
00:53:28.740 --> 00:53:33.463
So for a movement that wasn't after anyone specific.

1251
00:53:35.100 --> 00:53:36.920
There was no civil rights law they were after.

1252
00:53:36.920 --> 00:53:39.210
There was no permission to go to school type of thing

1253
00:53:39.210 --> 00:53:43.840
that the civil rights period had, which are very simple,

1254
00:53:43.840 --> 00:53:46.070
like really easy to understand,

1255
00:53:46.070 --> 00:53:47.370
things they're trying to accomplish

1256
00:53:47.370 --> 00:53:49.410
that makes it easier for spectators, I guess,

1257
00:53:49.410 --> 00:53:51.450
or other people in the public

1258
00:53:51.450 --> 00:53:55.532
who are sympathetic and wanna know.

1259
00:53:55.532 --> 00:53:57.890
The BLM movement didn't have that.

1260
00:53:57.890 --> 00:54:00.690
So it was kind of like harder to understand for some people.

1261
00:54:00.690 --> 00:54:01.840
But now we have these two

1262
00:54:01.840 --> 00:54:04.158
really concrete things, in my opinion.

1263
00:54:04.158 --> 00:54:04.991
What do you think about that?

1264
00:54:04.991 --> 00:54:07.210
Well, it's harder to calculate progress

1265
00:54:07.210 --> 00:54:09.730
without some kind of touchdown moment.

1266
00:54:09.730 --> 00:54:12.563
So on some level, that's what this represented.

1267
00:54:14.870 --> 00:54:17.330
And progress is iterative.

1268
00:54:17.330 --> 00:54:21.890
Despite how much kind of revolutionary energy

1269
00:54:21.890 --> 00:54:25.250
you have around massive change,

1270
00:54:25.250 --> 00:54:29.810
history dictates that these changes happen pretty slow.

1271
00:54:29.810 --> 00:54:34.750
And as much as some people would like it

1272
00:54:34.750 --> 00:54:37.020
to move much more quickly,

1273
00:54:37.020 --> 00:54:38.500
we have to at least acknowledge

1274
00:54:38.500 --> 00:54:41.750
that it is moving in the right direction.

1275
00:54:41.750 --> 00:54:42.583
It is.

1276
00:54:43.910 --> 00:54:46.000
A couple of questions for you,

1277
00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:50.730
because you talk with Jeremiah

1278
00:54:50.730 --> 00:54:54.620
about kind of the defund the police language.

1279
00:54:54.620 --> 00:54:59.620
And I think that you should lay out,

1280
00:54:59.712 --> 00:55:03.890
I know Jeremiah does very well, but people are confused.

1281
00:55:05.810 --> 00:55:08.550
I think that anytime you question the police,

1282
00:55:08.550 --> 00:55:11.070
it's been a third rail in this country for so long.

1283
00:55:11.070 --> 00:55:12.370
